WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:05.450
Throwing indestructible lizards into vats
of acid, hunting strange chicken men through

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:10.920
forests in Ireland, arguing in Latin with
a man wearing a haunted Roman Centurion’s

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.920
helmet.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:17.360
When you join the SCP Foundation, you might
be expecting high-octane drama all the time.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.650
Especially with the name Street Sweepers,
you’d expect this Mobile Task Force to be

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.120
neck deep in some real action-packed street
racing.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:30.509
Maybe you wouldn’t think that they’d be
tasked with driving all day every day in four-hour

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:35.860
shifts, tailing a semi-truck, all over Birmingham,
Alabama.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.970
But as Agent Moore and his colleague pulled
into the layby behind the truck, neither of

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.720
them were ready for what they were about to
witness…

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:44.720
*

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.780
SCP-2590 was first discovered by the Foundation
at a routine traffic stop.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.170
Investigating a totally different anomaly
in the Birmingham area, Agents Peters and

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:56.630
Smith had been posing as local police officers.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:00.989
The Foundation had been trying to track down
an artifact that was supposedly being smuggled

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:05.050
across the US in the back of a non-descript
station wagon.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:10.470
Peters and Smith had been allocated a pair
of beat-up old police cruisers which they’d

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.830
parked across the dirt road, fully blocking
any traffic from coming through.

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:19.720
It was several hours into their shift, when
the incident occurred, just at the point that

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.119
they were starting to lose focus.

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:26.840
Taking a look through the suitcases and memorabilia
from a family’s trip to Disney World, Peters

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.230
had taken way too long to hear the noise of
the engine swelling behind him.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:35.900
He spun around to see the hulking shape of
the semi-truck barreling straight towards

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:39.180
him, Agent Smith, and a family of five.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:43.130
With only two seconds to react, he yelled
out at the top of his lungs and dived out

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:48.170
of the way, leaving the trunk of the car wide
open with five screams emerging from inside.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:52.560
Smith, who had been sitting in one of the
cruisers, only just managed to get out before

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.520
the semi made contact.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:59.289
Eyes closed, Agent Peters waited for the inevitable
sound of screaming rubber, the bang of metal

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:02.590
on metal, and the shower of glass on asphalt.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:04.020
But it never came.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.220
When he opened his eyes, the station wagon
was still parked up in front of them, the

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:13.239
two police cruisers still blocking the road,
and all of the Disney merch still piled high

00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:14.290
in the trunk.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:19.700
The semi was driving off along the road on
the other side of their blockade, not a scratch

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.700
on it.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.500
Without a moment's hesitation, Agent Smith,
who had kept his eyes open and witnessed the

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.620
whole thing, leaped into action.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:31.360
He ordered his partner, still lying confused
in the dirt, to administer Class-A amnestics

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.110
to the family and call in for backup.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:38.610
Agent Smith himself jammed his keys into the
ignition, twisted them so hard he almost bent

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.720
the metal, and took off after the vehicle.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:46.430
What Agents Smith and Peters had just witnessed
was the very first Foundation exposure to

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:51.360
SCP-2590, fondly nicknamed Trailer Trash.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:56.110
As Smith pulled up alongside the vehicle and
studied it for the first time, he made a note

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:01.379
of its initial appearance over the radio,
an appearance which remains unchanged years

00:03:01.379 --> 00:03:02.379
later.

00:03:02.379 --> 00:03:07.269
The badges on the vehicle claim that it is
an International ProStar DayCab semi-trailer

00:03:07.269 --> 00:03:10.140
truck, complete with an unmarked trailer.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.490
As the Agent flicked on his lights and indicated
that the vehicle should pull over, he noted

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:18.970
that it didn’t have any license plates on
it, either front or rear.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:23.159
He leaned forward in his seat, trying to peer
into the cab to make out the driver, but in

00:03:23.159 --> 00:03:26.940
the Alabama sun, the man just looked like
a shadowy figure.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.660
They drove side by side along the road for
almost a mile.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:36.129
The truck made no signs of pulling over despite
Agent Smith’s continued insistence and repeated

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:40.989
flashes of the cop lights, but it also didn’t
attempt to pull away either.

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:45.780
It just continued to drive a few miles per
hour below the speed limit.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.220
The driver didn’t seem to look across at
him once.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:52.780
Having discussed it with Foundation staff,
they decided that it was best not to draw

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.790
attention to the situation.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:59.981
They had no idea whether this SCP was hostile
or posed any threat to civilian life, but

00:03:59.981 --> 00:04:03.890
having blue and red lights flashing at it
appeared to be doing little to change the

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:04.890
situation.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:10.269
Instead, he switched off the sirens and pulled
in behind the truck, tailing it around Birmingham

00:04:10.269 --> 00:04:14.430
as the Foundation readied further agents to
respond to the situation.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:17.430
For almost an hour, nothing of note happened.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.620
Agent Smith drove behind the trailer, watching
it like a hawk.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:26.090
He observed that it obeyed every traffic law
to a T. It never broke the speed limit, never

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.930
cut anyone off, and left room for other vehicles
to merge.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:34.150
If hadn’t seen it drive straight through
a roadblock as if it wasn’t there, he would

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:36.210
never have suspected a thing.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.980
But then the truck turned its turn signal
on.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.620
They had just come off the highway and merged
onto a quiet side street, just as the sun

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:45.990
was starting to hang low in the sky.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:51.500
The truck crept across to the side of the
road, squeezing its brakes gently, and stopped.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:56.460
Agent Smith matched the action the whole way,
pulling up about twenty feet behind the trailer.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.820
In constant radio communication, he kicked
open his door and stepped out into the evening

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:01.820
air.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:05.880
Foundation personnel advised that he keep
a hand on his gun at all times and approach

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:06.880
with caution.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.610
He didn’t really need them to tell him that.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.260
Smith called out for the driver to step out
of the cab.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.479
No response.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:17.300
The truck just sat there with its hazards
on, engine off.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:22.259
After a moment, there was a clunk, and the
trailer door started to slowly open, all by

00:05:22.259 --> 00:05:23.770
itself.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:27.160
Agent Smith called in backup, but they were
still several minutes out.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:31.880
Instead, he ran back to the car, gun raised,
and waited to see what was inside as the door

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:33.820
slowly opened to reveal…

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:34.820
Nothing.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.110
No, not quite nothing.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:40.410
There was something small on the floor of
the trailer, right in the center, as if it

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:43.180
hadn’t been moved around at all by the vehicle’s
motion.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:44.180
It was red.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:46.380
A kind of elongated cuboid.

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:51.180
He reported it all to the Foundation over
his radio, then paused when he recognized

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.180
what it was.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:54.220
A Kit Kat candy bar.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:58.400
Or, to be more specific, a Kit Kat Chunky.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.470
What happened after this point was hazy.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:04.660
Agent Smith was found on the roadside just
twenty minutes later, confused about what

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:05.690
had happened.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.650
The truck was nowhere in sight.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:11.880
However, a security camera from a convenience
store just up the street happened to capture

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.190
the interaction.

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:17.330
In the footage, you see Agent Smith approaching
the trailer with his gun raised, looking at

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:18.330
the Kit Kat.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:23.690
He tries to enter the trailer but is unable
to, so approaches the driver’s side door.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:27.910
While talking to the shadowy figure in the
cab, he drops his gun and stands motionless,

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:33.750
a confused and sleepy expression on his face,
until the trailer door closes and the SCP

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.090
drives away.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:41.069
Contact was reestablished with SCP-2590 soon
after and has been maintained almost uninterrupted

00:06:41.069 --> 00:06:42.370
ever since.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:47.590
The findings made on that initial encounter
seem to hold true across further examination.

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:52.759
Personnel has reached out to Navistar International,
the company that supposedly manufactures this

00:06:52.759 --> 00:06:57.630
model of semi-truck, but there appear to be
no records of its creation or shipment to

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:58.630
the US.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:04.870
In fact, no documentation at all can be attributed
to the truck or any components on it.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:10.139
The driver in the front cab is a humanoid
figure who is perpetually shrouded in shadow,

00:07:10.139 --> 00:07:13.840
designated SCP-2590-1.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:17.660
Attempts to reveal the driver’s features
have proven ineffective, as even powerful

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:22.840
spotlights do not shed enough light into the
cab to render the driver visible.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:28.860
Quite what this driver’s role is in the
operation of SCP-2590 is unknown.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:34.610
SCP-2590-1 appears to have some proximity-based
amnestic qualities, as anyone approaching

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:40.650
it on foot has reported memory loss and confusion
soon after, just like Agent Smith.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:45.630
As also discovered by the two agents and their
roadblock, containment of this SCP is simply

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:46.630
not possible.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:51.690
While the majority of the time, the SCP is
corporeal, it possesses the ability to pass

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:53.940
through solid objects at will.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:58.800
All attempted roadblocks have resulted in
the same thing happening, the SCP will just

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.479
phase right on through them as if nothing
was there.

00:08:02.479 --> 00:08:06.700
Since it cannot be contained in the usual
way, a different operation has been set up

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:11.710
to monitor the truck’s activities which
so far have proven to be apparently harmless

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:13.760
to the civilian population.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:18.870
Mobile Task Force Gamma 133, also known as
the street sweepers, has been established

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:22.880
to follow this SCP around Birmingham at all
times.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:27.940
They operate in four-hour shifts, with two
agents in unmarked vehicles sticking close

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.449
behind the trailer at all times.

00:08:30.449 --> 00:08:34.890
The Foundation was able to fit a tracking
device onto it as well, providing researchers

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:38.890
with continuous location data for where they
can find the vehicle.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:44.219
At seemingly random times, supposedly determined
by the SCP itself, it pulls over somewhere

00:08:44.219 --> 00:08:47.200
quiet and opens the door to its trailer.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:51.680
The door will remain open for 60 seconds,
and then close again.

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:56.550
Any attempts to enter the trailer have been
blocked by some kind of invisible barrier,

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:59.680
seemingly impenetrable to most approaches.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:04.050
More violent and destructive methods of entry
cannot be authorized for testing, due to the

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:07.589
heavy civilian population in the surrounding
area.

00:09:07.589 --> 00:09:11.950
Every time the doors open, there is something
different in the trailer.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:15.899
Researchers are trying to ascertain some kind
of pattern or messaging behind most of the

00:09:15.899 --> 00:09:18.579
objects, but many seem to be random.

00:09:18.579 --> 00:09:23.700
The current list of things that have appeared
in the back of SCP-2590 include an iPhone

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:29.779
3G, a red apple, and a lit lightbulb without
any visible form of power supply.

00:09:29.779 --> 00:09:35.010
Most notable about the objects in the trailer
is that often they appear to be human beings,

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:39.570
as happened on the night that Agent Moore
was on duty in the Street Sweepers.

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:40.570
*

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:44.060
The Agents pulled in behind the truck as per
usual when it slowed to a stop beside the

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:45.250
highway.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:49.530
Agent Moore got out of the vehicle second,
unenthused about the monotony of the task

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.150
that he had been assigned.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:55.220
Expecting to see a cardboard box or a chapstick
when the trailer door opened, he was left

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:59.320
shocked when he came face to face with himself.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:04.210
Few people can say that they have seen themselves
in real life, most of them have been administered

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:09.140
with various amnestics to make them forget,
but Agent Moore went on to report how bizarre

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:10.960
of an experience it was.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:15.339
He claimed that it was utterly unlike looking
in a mirror where your reflection is flipped

00:10:15.339 --> 00:10:17.390
and follows your every move.

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:22.410
Seeing yourself standing in three dimensions,
moving independently and evidently in a great

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:26.520
deal of distress, is an experience that few
would envy.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:30.790
Any time a human being materializes in the
trailer, they appear to be in a great deal

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:35.019
of distress as they attempt to escape through
the invisible barrier.

00:10:35.019 --> 00:10:40.130
Agent Moore and his partner Agent Hall could
do nothing but stand and watch in confusion

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:45.480
as the copy of him attempted to free himself
before, after the usual 60 seconds, the trailer

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:48.839
door closed, and the vehicle pulled away again.

00:10:48.839 --> 00:10:52.769
Several instances have occurred of duplicate
humans appearing in the trailer, but each

00:10:52.769 --> 00:10:57.380
time the ‘original’ person seems to have
had no knowledge of this taking place, and

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.790
nothing out of the ordinary happens to them.

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:04.580
However, there appears to be some small pattern
demonstrating the SCP has an awareness of

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:10.089
the Foundation as it has also duplicated Agent
Inglis’s sister, who has no connection to

00:11:10.089 --> 00:11:12.220
this SCP at all.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:16.910
Incident 16 was the most distressing of all,
as a large slab of metal appeared in the back

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:21.170
of the trailer with the SCP Foundation logo
painted across it.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:25.540
Agents Inglis and Shultz were on duty at the
time and observed copious amounts of blood

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:27.660
flowing out of the metal slab.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:31.889
Before long, the blood filled the back of
the trailer, pushing up against the invisible

00:11:31.889 --> 00:11:32.889
barrier.

00:11:32.889 --> 00:11:38.329
All of a sudden, 52 seconds into the encounter,
the barrier vanished, and a cascade of blood

00:11:38.329 --> 00:11:43.920
with the slab inside were launched out at
the two agents at a speed of over 190 kilometers

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:47.209
an hour, killing them both instantly.

00:11:47.209 --> 00:11:52.430
Since this incident, SCP-2590 has been treated
with greater caution.

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:57.320
The most mysterious thing to have come from
researching this truck came on December 4th,

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:02.490
2011, when for the first time, the truck’s
tracking beacon stopped working.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:06.680
It had been seen pulling into an abandoned
warehouse and so a team of Street Sweepers

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:08.690
was immediately dispatched to investigate.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:13.470
When they arrived, they found the vehicle
moving through the warehouse at a slow crawl.

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:18.120
Choosing to pursue on foot and leaving a pair
of agents at the entrance, they followed the

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:23.769
SCP through the facility until it came to
what agents described as a ‘service tunnel

00:12:23.769 --> 00:12:25.470
or sewer of some sort’.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:30.380
Putting headlamps on, they followed the truck
down into the tunnel, maintaining radio contact

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:31.380
throughout.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:35.579
As they reported the direction they were traveling
and the distance, it quickly became apparent

00:12:35.579 --> 00:12:39.350
to Foundation personnel that this was no ordinary
tunnel.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:44.670
The warehouse was positioned overlooking a
cliff, and so the geography was not physically

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:45.740
possible.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:49.680
As the Street Sweepers descended further into
the tunnel, they noted that there were increased

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:51.860
levels of carbon monoxide.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:57.060
Radio contact started to dip in and out, losing
signal as they went further downhill.

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:01.360
Just at the edge of their signal with the
Foundation, the truck stopped and opened its

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:02.940
trailer door.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:07.500
Inside was just a single piece of parchment
with the words ‘I'm just delivering a message’

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:08.640
written on it.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:13.420
After the usual 60 seconds, the trailer door
closed, and the truck continued.

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:17.550
After they had passed the kilometer mark,
the radio signal worsened quickly, and after

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:22.010
a couple of scrambled messages, the team down
there were not heard from again.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:26.190
The channel stayed open for another 6 hours
before the Foundation made the decision to

00:13:26.190 --> 00:13:28.839
announce the agents missing in action.

00:13:28.839 --> 00:13:34.769
In March 2015, over three years later, a radio
signal came into contact with the Foundation

00:13:34.769 --> 00:13:37.380
again from Birmingham, Alabama.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:41.230
It was from the headset of the squad leader
who had gone into the tunnel.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:45.580
Initially confused as to who had gained access
to the comms channel, the Foundation demanded

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:48.300
that the agent state his full name and rank.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:52.779
The agent, himself confused, obliged, questioning
why they were so suspicious.

00:13:52.779 --> 00:13:57.200
He and his team claimed to have only lost
contact for about fifteen minutes.

00:13:57.200 --> 00:14:01.470
They had followed the SCP a little further
until carbon monoxide levels had risen too

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:05.649
high to continue, at which point they’d
had to watched the truck disappearing into

00:14:05.649 --> 00:14:08.579
the distance as they walked back to the surface.

00:14:08.579 --> 00:14:14.080
All agents have undergone extensive psychological
rehabilitation to settle them back into society,

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:19.290
as well as classes to fill them in on things
like the London Olympics, the Ice Bucket Challenge,

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.300
and Gangnam style.

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:28.790
As for SCP-2590, it is back out on the roads,
roaming around Birmingham, Alabama continuously.

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:33.680
Never stopping for fuel, always obeying the
rules of the road, occasionally opening its

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.610
trailer doors to reveal new and bizarre findings…

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:43.870
Now check out “Living Ice Cream Van SCP-1386”
and “SCP-342 - A Ticket to Ride” for more!

